  authors/documents, and generates a bibliography in a user-chosen format.
    - ProgrammingST22-Final1 RELATES_TO Author uniqueness and ordering: ProgrammingST22-Final1
  defines authors as uniquely identified by the combination of first name and last name
  (case-sensitive); author order in a publication is the order in which authors are added and
  determines positions like first author.
    - ProgrammingST22-Final1 RELATES_TO Article (Publication type): ProgrammingST22-Final1 models a
  Publication type 'Article' that requires an id (lowercase letters and digits), a title, a
  publication year, and at least one author; each article has exactly one publication venue.
    - ProgrammingST22-Final1 RELATES_TO Citation styles 'acm' and 'apa': ProgrammingST22-Final1
  requires implementing two bibliography styles 'acm' and 'apa' with the specified simplified
  formatting templates for conference and journal articles.
    - ProgrammingST22-Final1 RELATES_TO Bibliography sorting order: ProgrammingST22-Final1 specifies
   a deterministic bibliography sorting order comparing first-author last name, first name, second
  author names, …, then title, year, and finally publication identifier; missing n-th author sorts
  before present n-th author.
    - ProgrammingST22-Final1 RELATES_TO Reference year restriction: ProgrammingST22-Final1 allows
  publications to reference only publications with a strictly earlier publication year.
    - ProgrammingST22-Final1 RELATES_TO Keyword rules and inheritance: ProgrammingST22-Final1
  enforces keywords to be lowercase letters only, prohibits special characters, and implements
  keyword inheritance (series→conference→article and journal→article) with duplicates deduplicated.
    - ProgrammingST22-Final1 RELATES_TO Case-sensitive uniqueness rule for identifiers:
  ProgrammingST22-Final1 requires entity identifiers to be case-sensitive and forbids creating an
  entity with an already-used unique identifier (identifiers distinguish by case).
    - ProgrammingST22-Final1 RELATES_TO Conference/Series/Journal model: ProgrammingST22-Final1
  models ConferenceSeries, Conference, and Journal: series and journals are uniquely identified by
  type+name; a Conference is identified by its series and year; a Journal always has exactly one
  publisher; at most one conference per series per year.
